  "question": {
    "text": "When a salt is treated with sodium hydroxide solution it gives gas $\\mathrm{X}$. On passing gas $\\mathrm{X}$ through reagent $\\mathrm{Y}$ a brown coloured precipitate is formed. $\\mathrm{X}$ and $\\mathrm{Y}$ respectively, are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Z0RIP",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{X}=\\mathrm{NH}_3$ and $\\mathrm{Y}=\\mathrm{HgO}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "uiC64",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{X}=\\mathrm{NH}_3$ and $\\mathrm{Y}=\\mathrm{K}_2 \\mathrm{HgI}_4+\\mathrm{KOH}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ul0Vl",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{X}=\\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{Cl}$ and $\\mathrm{Y}=\\mathrm{KOH}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CQWkL",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{X}=\\mathrm{HCl}$ and $\\mathrm{Y}=\\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{Cl}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{NH}_4^{+}+\\mathrm{NaOH} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}+\\mathrm{NH}_3 \\uparrow$<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/zlgVoLdTpziORH65aQ1uy2tTAdVeTZrPImGlJs1cJ0o.original.fullsize.png\"/><br />$\\mathrm{NH}_3$ is identify by $\\mathrm{K}_2\\left[\\mathrm{HgI}_4\\right]+\\mathrm{KOH}$",
